On 7 Sep 2011, at 6:17, Bob LeChevalier, President and Founder - LLG  
wrote:
> So there is no specific name for the test that says that "paigli'u"  
> is invalid, because it could break up into "pai gli'u".

Actually, "{gli'u}" fails the {slinku'i} test (cf. "{togli'u}" et  
alii) and so is not a valid word, which should mean that it has to  
"absorb" the syllable before it, making "{paigli'u}" a valid single  
{fu'ivla}.  I once wrote a (complete?) description of a/the word  
splitting algorithm that covers this:
<https://github.com/jwodder/jbobaf/blob/master/share/tadji/lerfendi.txt>

mu'omi'e .kamymecraijun.

